# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hermes-stack — files that must NEVER reach a public repo, plus local state.
#
# RULE OF THUMB: this repo tracks the RECIPE (Dockerfiles, compose, scripts,
# templates). It does not track SECRETS, DATA, or anything an agent wrote.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The single most important line in this file. .env holds the WebUI password,
# the Cloudflare tunnel token, dashboard credentials, LLM API keys and the IDE
# connection token. Committing it is a full compromise of the deployment.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
credentials.json
auth.json

# --- Persistent agent state (Filip's data, not source) ---------------------
# hermes-home is every profile's config, conversation database, memory and
# credentials — tens of thousands of files and all five bots' private history.
hermes-home/

# The agents' working checkouts. These are SEPARATE git repos with their own
# remotes; committing them here would nest repos and leak private code.
workspace/

# The Obsidian knowledge base. Real notes, not deployment recipe.
wiki/

# --- Runtime IPC -----------------------------------------------------------
# Unix domain sockets for the ACP relays. Sockets are not files git can store
# (`archive/tar: sockets not supported`) and are recreated on every boot.
acp-ipc/
*.sock

# --- Backups produced by the IDE reseed ------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak.*

# --- Local editor / OS noise ----------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Logs and scratch ------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
tmp/
